---
// Unlisted page (11.12.26): not in the nav, the sitemap or llms.txt, and
// marked noindex. Shared by direct link only.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const steps = [
    ["Start from my own words.", "The narration is taken from the story itself, passage by passage. Where a line needs to be shorter, I cut or join my own sentences; nothing is paraphrased or invented."],
    ["Plan every shot in one file.", "Each 8 to 10 second shot is written down once: its narration, what is on screen, the action second by second, what it must show and must not show, continuity and sound. The script, captions and video prompts are all generated from that one file, so a change in one place carries everywhere."],
    ["Draft with AI, direct myself.", "I work with Claude, Anthropic's AI, to draft the shot list and prompts. I choose the passages, make the edits and decide what stays."],
    ["Hold a house style.", "A style document I keep goes into every prompt, along with each film's own look. For Starkite, that is cyanotype star charts for space and warm lamplight for home."],
    ["Check the plan before generating.", "A separate AI reviewer reads the shots against the source. Pictures make claims too, so it checks what each image would imply, not just the words."],
    ["Make reference images first.", "Characters, key objects and a style plate are generated before any video and attached to the shots, so faces and the look hold from shot to shot."],
    ["Generate the shots.", "Clips are made with Google's Gemini Omni Flash, mostly in batches through its API. When a prompt is refused or keeps missing, I rework it and make that shot by hand; Starkite's opening and title were made this way."],
    ["Check every shot against its plan.", "Each clip is compared frame by frame with what it must show. Misses, such as photographs that should age and don't, or an alien planet that looks like Jupiter, are rewritten and retaken. Every take is kept."],
    ["Assemble.", "The chosen takes are joined with the title and captions into a rough cut. Narration is recorded last, over the finished picture."],
];
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Animation - Claire Nyquist"
    description="Short animated films by Claire Nyquist: a story and a research explainer."
    noindex={true}
>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl name-gradient mb-6">Animation</h1>
            <p class="text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
                Short animated films I write, direct and edit, made with generative video and a repeatable process
                that keeps every line true to its source.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section id="starkite" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-20">
            <header class="mb-6 text-center">
                <h2 class="font-space-grotesk text-3xl md:text-4xl text-gray-900 mb-3">Starkite</h2>
                <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600">A story by Claire Nyquist</p>
                <p class="text-gray-500 italic mt-3">
                    A wafer-sized probe is flung at the nearest star, and one founder lives long enough to see the data come home.
                </p>
            </header>
            <video
                src="/videos/animation/starkite.mp4"
                poster="/images/animation/starkite-poster.webp"
                controls
                playsinline
                preload="metadata"
                width="1280"
                height="720"
                aria-label="Animated short film of the story Starkite, with captions."
                class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg shadow-lg"
            ></video>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">
                Rough cut with captions; narration to come. The words are from my story
                <a href="/fiction#starkite" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Starkite</a>.
                Visuals generated with Gemini Omni Flash.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="deep-pareto" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-20">
            <header class="mb-6 text-center">
                <h2 class="font-space-grotesk text-3xl md:text-4xl text-gray-900 mb-3">Balancing Competing Goals</h2>
                <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600">Research explainer, draft</p>
                <p class="text-gray-500 italic mt-3">
                    How a recommender that learns each viewer's balance of goals raised three of them at once.
                </p>
            </header>
            <video
                src="/videos/animation/deep-pareto.mp4"
                poster="/images/animation/deep-pareto-poster.webp"
                controls
                playsinline
                preload="metadata"
                width="1280"
                height="720"
                aria-label="Animated draft explainer of a research paper on multi-objective recommender systems, with captions."
                class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg shadow-lg"
            ></video>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">
                An independent explainer of Li and Tuzhilin (2026),
                <i>Deep Pareto Reinforcement Learning for Multi-Objective Recommender Systems</i>,
                MIS Quarterly 50(3), 1087–1116,
                <a href="https://doi.org/10.25300/MISQ/2025/19488" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">doi.org/10.25300/MISQ/2025/19488</a>.
                Draft rough cut with captions; narration to come. Scripted from the authors' full preprint and not yet
                reviewed by them. Not affiliated with MIS Quarterly. Visuals generated with Gemini Omni Flash.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="process" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
            <h2 class="font-space-grotesk text-2xl md:text-3xl text-gray-900 mb-6 text-center">How It Was Made</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-800">
                {steps.map(([title, text]) => (
                    <li><b>{title}</b> {text}</li>
                ))}
            </ol>
        </section>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
